save(136,dict(paragraphs=["Kaberi Chattopadhyaya, published as Kaberi Chattopadhyay, grew up in Assam and taught English in West Bengal. Her writing includes the memoir Peeping Through My Window, the poetry collection The Twilight Bells and short fiction. Her publisher’s account connects an education at Calcutta University and North Eastern Hill University with a teaching career at Ramkrishna Vivekananda Mission and Army Public School, Barrackpore.","Her Kabita Live poems often pause at moments when a life changes its shape. ‘The silver bathed night’ observes a father facing retirement; ‘DUKHIRAM’ discovers a labouring boy’s lost childhood in a kaleidoscope. ‘Love`s First Rays’ attends to an unexpected awakening of affection, while ‘AS LIFE DEMANDS’ turns towards the ethical choices people make in a world of unequal joys and sorrows."],sources=[source('Penprints — The Twilight Bells','https://penprints.in/shop/product/the-twilight-bells-by-kaberi-chattopadhyay/',['Assam upbringing; universities; English teaching; memoir; poetry collection, 2022, ISBN 9788195619771']),source('Penprints — Apparitions from the Other World','https://penprints.in/shop/product/apparitions-from-the-other-world-by-kaberi-chattopadhyay/',['Short-fiction work and matching author biography'])],books=[dict(title='The Twilight Bells',detail='Poetry · Penprints, 2022',url='https://penprints.in/shop/product/the-twilight-bells-by-kaberi-chattopadhyay/')],identity_match='Publisher matches Assam background, both universities, both teaching institutions and exact memoir/poetry titles despite final-a surname variant.',poems_read=[dict(id=469,title='AS LIFE DEMANDS',basis='Full source read: joy/sorrow, moral contrasts and collective honesty.'),dict(id=335,title='DUKHIRAM',basis='Full source read: young labourer, masonry, simple meal and kaleidoscope recovering childhood.'),dict(id=254,title='Love`s First Rays',basis='Full source read: weary routine transformed by unexpected touch and affection.'),dict(id=115,title='The silver bathed night',basis='Full source read: father after retirement celebration, pride, uncertainty and shared pain.')],limitations=['Supplied biography preserved; sensitive health detail not repeated in new narrative.','Poetic father and daughter references are described as scenes, not independently established family facts.','Publisher main-shop search result contains conflicting adjacent 2023 metadata; specific 2022 title page and matching ISBN used.','Stray source markup in poem 115 remains unchanged.'],next_action='Independent author/editor review of surname display and prose.'))
